            <ArticleTitle>Mechanical Alloying of Metal-Organic Frameworks.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2413-2417</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/anie.201612587</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The solvent-free mechanical milling process for two distinct metal-organic framework (MOF) crystals induced the formation of a solid solution, which is not feasible by conventional solution-based syntheses. X-ray and STEM-EDX studies revealed that performing mechanical milling under an Ar atmosphere promotes the high diffusivity of each metal ion in an amorphous solid matrix; the amorphous state turns into the porous crystalline structure by vapor exposure treatment to form a new phase of a MOF solid solution.</AbstractText>
